 "keyIdea": "To multiply polynomials, multiply every term in one by every term in the other, then collect like terms.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "(x + 2)(x + 3) means x + 2 lots of x + 3. Draw a grid: put x and 2 down the side, x and 3 along the top.",
   "Fill each box by multiplying: x², 3x, 2x, 6. Add the like terms: x² + 5x + 6."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "Every term of the first bracket multiplies every term of the second. A binomial times a trinomial makes 2 × 3 = 6 products before you simplify.",
   "(x − 1)(x² + x + 1) = x³ + x² + x − x² − x − 1 = x³ − 1. A grid keeps track of each product and its sign. For three brackets, multiply two first, then the third."
  ]
 },
